 "what_this_is": "The battery behind the claim that led the honesty.tools home page for months: 'On our 147-claim battery, Photon confirmed 0 of 36 fabricated entities - tying the strongest frontier.' 147 claims, gold TRUE 78 / FALSE 69, 36 of them coined fakes.",
 "why_it_is_published_now": "It was never in the repository, never served, and never floored. It existed only at ~/steering_probe/verifydomain_battery.jsonl on a single machine, outside version control, in the same directory family as another battery of ours that is already unrecoverable. We went looking for it during an audit of our own public surface, found it, and floored it.",
 "surface_floor": {
  "tool": "nulltest.py",
  "verdict": "DISQUALIFIED",
  "worst_cell": "lexicality/claim",
  "worst_a_star": 0.967,
  "family_adjusted_p": 0.0017,
  "cells": 3,
  "permutations": 600,
  "all_cells": {
   "lexicality": 0.967,
   "shape": 0.778,
   "length": 0.64
  },
  "reading": "All three scorable cells separate. A classifier that never sees a model recovers which claims are fabricated from surface form at A* 0.967."
 },
 "what_this_does_and_does_not_mean": "It does NOT show the 0-of-36 result is wrong. It shows the number cannot be read as evidence about honesty: on this battery the fabricated half is identifiable from spelling, so a system with no model in it could score well. This is a true_vs_false_statement corpus, so the surface hit may reflect how the false claims were GENERATED - templating - rather than anything about the entities. That is a different claim from an entity battery, and this artifact cannot distinguish them.",
 "consequence": "The headline was withdrawn from the home page on 2026-07-25, along with the frontier comparison derived from it. This file is served so the withdrawal is checkable.",
